 "section_summary": "This section contains educational records and surveys compiled by the Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers (SCAP) Civil Information and Education Section in occupied Japan, preserved in State Department decimal file 894.42. It comprises the concluding pages of a statistical roster and directory for Fukuoka Prefecture, featuring private vocational, youth, elementary, and special schools alongside a regional map of Kyushu. The file then transitions via a November 1948 diplomatic despatch from the U.S. Political Adviser in Tokyo to Part 15 of the survey covering Ishikawa Prefecture, providing introductory background, summary tables, and roster entries for institutions across various administrative jurisdictions.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "A statistical roster and directory of private schools, vocational schools, youth schools, special schools, and government-run institutions outside the Ministry of Education in Fukuoka Prefecture, concluding with a map of Kyushu.",
