   ],
   "start_page": 109,
   "summary": "This document constitutes the concluding portion of the Fukuoka Prefecture section of the SCAP Civil Information and Education Section roster of Japanese educational institutions. It provides statistical tables and directory entries for private secondary, elementary, and special vocational schools, as well as schools operated by ministries other than the Ministry of Education as of April and November 1946. Listed institutions include youth schools attached to factories and mines, domestic science schools, language institutes, nurse training schools, and juvenile correction facilities across Fukuoka Prefecture. The section concludes with an educational map of Kyushu highlighting prefectural capitals, major cities, and institutions of higher learning.",
   "title": "Roster of Japanese Educational Institutions: Fukuoka Prefecture",
   "to": ""
  },
