   "start_page": 139,
   "summary": "This special report prepared by SCAP's Civil Information and Education Section provides a comprehensive directory and statistical analysis of educational institutions in Ishikawa Prefecture for April and November 1946. It includes an administrative introduction explaining the scope, methodology, and Japanese school system jurisdictions, followed by prefectural summary tables categorizing institutions, students, and teachers by level, type, and control. Part Three begins the detailed roster listing individual institutions under Ministry of Education and prefectural control, including universities, colleges, higher schools, normal schools, vocational schools, and middle schools. The report documents school foundation dates, locations, student enrollment, and faculty numbers divided by gender and employment status.",
